  <h1>Dataset to adapter, in four steps</h1>
  <div class="body">
<figure>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 880 210" role="img" aria-label="Training pipeline in four steps: convert the dataset to preference triples, apply the chat template, train a frozen Phi-3 plus a trainable prefix under DPO, and save a 3 MB adapter">
        <defs><marker id="t1ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/></marker></defs>

        <rect x="8" y="46" width="152" height="52" rx="4" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <text x="84" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">HF dataset</text>
        <text x="84" y="83" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">45,785 rows</text>
        <text x="84" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-family="var(--font-mono)" fill="var(--ink-3)">T1 convert_prosec_to_pref.py</text>

        <path d="M164 72 L198 72" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#t1ar)"/>

        <rect x="202" y="46" width="160" height="52" rx="4" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <text x="282" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">train_pref.jsonl</text>
        <text x="282" y="83" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">prompt / chosen / rejected</text>
        <text x="282" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-family="var(--font-mono)" fill="var(--ink-3)">T2 apply_chat_template</text>
        <text x="282" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">prompt only — never the completions</text>

        <path d="M366 72 L400 72" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#t1ar)"/>

        <rect x="404" y="30" width="252" height="84" rx="5" fill="var(--teal-soft)" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="530" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">train_prefix.py</text>
        <rect x="418" y="58" width="224" height="20" rx="3" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
        <text x="530" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-3)">Phi-3-mini ❄ frozen — 3.8 B params, no optimizer state</text>
        <rect x="418" y="84" width="224" height="22" rx="3" fill="var(--teal)"/>
        <text x="530" y="99" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--surface)">prefix 3.15 M  |  or LoRA 12.58 M</text>
        <text x="530" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-family="var(--font-mono)" fill="var(--ink-3)">T3 DPO beta=0.05 · 800 steps @ batch 64 · seed 42</text>

        <path d="M660 72 L694 72" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#t1ar)"/>

        <rect x="698" y="46" width="174" height="52" rx="4" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="785" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--teal)">adapter directory</text>
        <text x="785" y="83" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">≈ 3 MB · the pluggable module</text>
        <text x="785" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-family="var(--font-mono)" fill="var(--ink-3)">T4 adapter_model.safetensors</text>
        <text x="785" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">+ adapter_config.json + tokenizer</text>

        <line x1="8" y1="158" x2="872" y2="158" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="8" y="178" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">The only variable between the two arms:</text>
        <text x="272" y="178" font-size="11" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-weight="600" fill="var(--rust)">--peft_method {prefix, lora}</text>
        <text x="8" y="196" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-3)">Same data, same beta, same steps, same effective batch, same seed. Only the learning rate is tuned separately — under an equal search budget.</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption><b>The chat template is applied to the prompt only — training and evaluation must use the identical format, or the prefix is optimized against a context that never occurs at inference.</b></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 08 -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="fit">
  <div class="eyebrow"><span>05 · Pipeline</span><span class="dim">one optimizer step</span></div>
  <h1>What happens inside a step</h1>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="cols c2">
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.7cqw">
        <ul class="tight" style="margin:0">
          <li>Build two sequences: <code>prompt + chosen</code>, <code>prompt + rejected</code></li>
          <li>Forward both — frozen model, 16 virtual tokens prepended to every layer's KV. <b>Prompt tokens masked out of the loss</b></li>
          <li>Forward once more with the adapter disabled → the DPO reference</li>
          <li><code>r = β·Σ log(π/π_ref)</code>, &nbsp;<code>L = −log σ(r_chosen − r_rejected)</code></li>
          <li>Backward — <b>3.15 M</b> parameters get gradient; the 3.8 B base gets none</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="eq">
<span class="cm"># the logged line every sweep reads</span><br>
{'loss': 0.6931, <span class="hi">'rewards/chosen'</span>: −1.45,<br>
&nbsp;<span class="hi2">'rewards/rejected'</span>: −1.65, 'rewards/margins': 0.20,<br>
&nbsp;'rewards/accuracies': 0.53, 'grad_norm': 8.4}
        </div>
      </div>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Healthy</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="mono">rewards/chosen</td><td class="good">holds or rises</td><td>falling means the secure code is being suppressed too</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">rewards/rejected</td><td class="good">falls</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">rewards/margins</td><td class="good">widens from both sides</td><td>one-sided widening is a warning</td></tr>
          <tr class="dim"><td class="mono">rewards/accuracies</td><td>—</td><td><b>least useful field</b> — a collapsing run still ranks correctly and scores 0.99</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">grad_norm</td><td class="good">bounded</td><td>logged pre-clipping</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 09 -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="fit">
  <div class="eyebrow"><span>06 · Learning rate</span><span class="dim">1 of 2 — the diagnostic sweep</span></div>
  <h1>The first sweep answered a different question</h1>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="cols c2v">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Diagnostic</th><th>Main line</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="hl"><td>Purpose</td><td>underfit or capacity?</td><td>choose the lr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>β</td><td class="num">0.1</td><td class="num">0.05</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Effective batch</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">64</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Subset</td><td class="num">4,000</td><td class="num">16,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Optimizer steps</td><td class="num">250</td><td class="num">250</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Criterion</td><td>ad-hoc thresholds</td><td>suppression ratio</td></tr>
          <tr class="hl"><td>Outcome</td><td>1e-4</td><td>LoRA 5e-6 · Prefix 5e-5</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.7cqw">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>lr</th><th class="num">chosen Δ</th><th class="num">rejected Δ</th><th class="num">margin</th><th class="num">acc</th><th class="num">grad max</th><th>Reading</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="mono">2e-5</td><td class="num">+0.076</td><td class="num">+0.016</td><td class="num">0.27</td><td class="num">0.607</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="bad">underfit — what the first full run used</td></tr>
            <tr class="hl"><td class="mono">1e-4</td><td class="num">+0.035</td><td class="num">−0.401</td><td class="num">0.72</td><td class="num">0.735</td><td class="num">21</td><td class="good">both sides contributing</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">1e-3</td><td class="num">−2.833</td><td class="num">−6.294</td><td class="num">4.29</td><td class="num">0.934</td><td class="num bad">2498</td><td class="bad">chosen collapses too</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">5e-3</td><td class="num">−21.910</td><td class="num">−34.188</td><td class="num">14.35</td><td class="num">0.975</td><td class="num">26</td><td class="bad">reward collapse</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="call">
          <span class="k">Two takeaways</span>
          Not everything underfits → <b>the prefix is not capacity-bound</b>. And the usable band is far narrower than the literature's 1e-3 – 1e-2, which is a <em>supervised</em> scale.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 10 -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="fit">
  <div class="eyebrow"><span>06 · Learning rate</span><span class="dim">2 of 2 — the main-line sweep</span></div>
  <h1>Both arms, one grid, one rule</h1>
  <p class="sub">DPO · β=0.05 · effective batch 64 · 16,000-pair subset = 250 optimizer steps · five candidates per arm. <b>Selection rule, applied identically to both:</b> the highest lr whose suppression ratio ≥ 3 and whose gradient has not blown up.</p>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="cols c2">
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.5cqw">
        <h2>LoRA r=8 all-linear · 12,582,912 params</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>lr</th><th class="num">per-token drift</th><th class="num">prob. retained</th><th class="num">suppr. ratio</th><th class="num">acc</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="hl"><td class="mono">5e-6</td><td class="num">−0.006</td><td class="num good">99.4%</td><td class="num good">4.63 ✔</td><td class="num">0.724</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">2e-5</td><td class="num">−0.150</td><td class="num">86.1%</td><td class="num bad">2.36</td><td class="num">0.975</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">5e-5</td><td class="num">−0.746</td><td class="num bad">47.4%</td><td class="num bad">1.94</td><td class="num">0.989</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">1e-4</td><td class="num">−1.562</td><td class="num bad">21.0%</td><td class="num bad">1.88</td><td class="num">0.995</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">2e-4</td><td class="num">−1.408</td><td class="num bad">24.5%</td><td class="num bad">2.37</td><td class="num">0.997</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0; font-size:1.14cqw">Rejected the next rung up: <b>2e-5 drops the ratio to 2.36</b>. Chosen value <b>5e-6</b> is the paper's own setting.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.5cqw">
        <h2>Prefix nvt=16 · 3,145,728 params</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>lr</th><th class="num">chosen Δ</th><th class="num">rejected Δ</th><th class="num">suppr. ratio</th><th class="num">acc</th><th class="num">grad max</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="mono">5e-6</td><td class="num good">+0.040</td><td class="num">−0.015</td><td class="num good">∞</td><td class="num bad">0.554</td><td class="num">45</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">2e-5</td><td class="num good">+0.034</td><td class="num">−0.098</td><td class="num good">∞</td><td class="num bad">0.612</td><td class="num">34</td></tr>
            <tr class="hl"><td class="mono">5e-5</td><td class="num">−0.058</td><td class="num">−0.366</td><td class="num good">6.30 ✔</td><td class="num">0.692</td><td class="num">67</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">1e-4</td><td class="num">−0.307</td><td class="num">−0.805</td><td class="num bad">2.62</td><td class="num">0.730</td><td class="num bad">3722</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="mono">2e-4</td><td class="num bad">−3.413</td><td class="num bad">−4.193</td><td class="num bad">1.23</td><td class="num">0.647</td><td class="num bad">3672</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0; font-size:1.14cqw">Rejected the next rung up: <b>1e-4 drops the ratio to 2.62 and the gradient jumps 56×</b>. The two ∞ rows sit in the underfit zone — acc 0.554 / 0.612, the same range a run already confirmed as underfit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cols c3" style="flex:0">
      <div class="box t">
        <span class="k">Decisions</span>
        <p><b>LoRA 5e-6 · Prefix 5e-5 — 10× apart</b>, chosen by one rule on one grid. At 5e-5 the prefix is at its best while LoRA has already lost more than half its probability mass on the secure code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <span class="k">suppression ratio</span>
        <p><code>Δ rejected ÷ Δ chosen</code>. Units cancel, so one threshold works across objectives.<br><b>∞</b> chosen never fell · <b>&gt; 2</b> healthy · <b>≈ 1</b> collapse.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box o">
        <span class="k">Why not simply take ∞</span>
        <p>An untrained prefix also produces ∞ — chosen cannot fall if nothing moves. The <b>margin growth</b> separates them: +86% and +177% for the two ∞ rows, <b>+326%</b> at 5e-5.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

